# NOT ignored: /public/build
#
# The compiled frontend is committed on purpose. Hostinger shared hosting has
# no Node, so `npm run build` cannot run on the server, and @vite reads
# public/build/manifest.json at runtime -- without it Laravel throws a hard 500
# on every page, not merely an unstyled one. Committing the build output is what
# makes `git pull` a complete deployment.
#
# The cost is a diff in public/build on every release. Run `npm run build`
# before committing a frontend change, or the deployed CSS/JS goes stale.
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db

# Browser tests (F30). The Dusk environment file IS committed — it holds no
# real credentials and every integration in it is deliberately unconfigured —
# but its database and its failure artifacts are local noise.
/database/dusk.sqlite
/tests/Browser/screenshots
/tests/Browser/console
/tests/Browser/source
